{title: Walk in the Law}
{subtitle: Psalms 119:1–2}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Blessed are those whose way is blameless
[Ab]Who walk in the law of [Eb]the Lord
They keep [Ab]his testimonies [Cm]so
And [Ab]seek him with their [Bb]whole heart's [Eb]core
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Blessed are [Ab]those who walk in the [Eb]law
Blessed [Cm]are those who keep his [Bb]word
Blessed are [Ab]those who walk in the [Cm]law
Blessed are [Ab]those who [Bb]keep his [Eb]word
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Indeed they do [Bb]no wrong [Eb]at [Ab]all
They walk in his ways on [Eb]the ground
[Ab]You have laid down your [Bb]pre[Cm]cepts there
[Ab]To be kept with [Bb]care in ev[Eb]ery place
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Ab]Blessed are those who walk [Eb]in the law
Blessed [Cm]are those who keep his [Bb]word
Blessed [Ab]are those who walk in [Cm]the law
Blessed are [Ab]those who [Bb]keep his [Eb]word
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Eb] | [Ab] | [Eb] | [Cm7] |
| [Bb] | [Ab] | [Cm7] | [Ab] [Bb] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Oh that my ways were steady
[Ab]In keeping your statutes [Eb]true
My [Ab]heart would [Bb]find its rest [Cm7]then
In [Ab]what your [Bb]spirit has [Eb]done
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Blessed are [Ab]those who walk in the [Eb]law
Blessed [Ab]are those who keep his [Bb]word
{end_of_verse}
